--TEST--
`#[Core\Path]` on a parameter that is not a `string`, or on a declaration that takes no argument, is refused rather than ignored, and on a `string` or `?string` parameter it is accepted — `rule:programs/relative-paths-resolve-from-their-file`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:programs/file-paths-a-literal-starts-at-the-folder-of-its-file
// The marker says that a string literal passed to the parameter is a file
// path. An `int` parameter is never passed one.
class Counter {
    public static function bump(#[Core\Path] int $by): int { return $by + 1; }
}

// A property is never passed an argument at all.
class Settings {
    #[Core\Path]
    public string $file = '';
}

// The accepted sites: a `string` parameter and a `?string` one.
class Store {
    public static function load(#[Core\Path] string $file, #[Core\Path] ?string $backup = null): string {
        return $file;
    }
}

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0836]: `#[Core\Path] $by` is on a parameter of type `int`
  --> case.nvs:6:35
%A
error[E0836]: `#[Core\Path]` is on a property
   --> case.nvs:11:7
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
